# 2. OVERALL DESCRIPTION

## 2.1 Product Perspective

Property Partner shall be a responsive web application that integrates property discovery, AI-assisted services, and buyer–seller communication.

The prototype shall demonstrate the main workflows using realistic sample data and functional frontend interactions. Backend services, real AI processing, production authentication, and real payments shall be integrated only when explicitly configured.

## 2.2 User Classes

### 2.2.1 Guest User
- Browse public property listings.
- View property details.
- Explore available services.
- Register or log in.

### 2.2.2 Buyer
- Search and filter properties.
- View property details.
- Save favorite properties.
- Compare properties.
- Use AI Property Matchmaker.
- Use AI Property Designer.
- Purchase or simulate an AI Connect plan.
- Communicate with sellers when access is available.
- Manage profile information.

### 2.2.3 Seller
- Create a property listing.
- Upload property photographs.
- Enter property information.
- Edit or remove listings.
- View listing status.
- Receive and respond to buyer inquiries.
- Manage profile information.

### 2.2.4 Real Estate Agent
- Manage multiple property listings.
- View buyer inquiries.
- Update listing information.
- Manage professional profile details.

### 2.2.5 Administrator
- View users and property listings.
- Review reported content.
- Manage listing approval status.
- Review platform activity and subscription records.

Administrative operations may be demonstrated through sample data in the prototype.

## 2.3 Operating Environment

- Frontend: React and TypeScript.
- Development platform: Lovable.
- Styling: Tailwind CSS.
- Components: reusable UI component library.
- Icons: Lucide icons.
- Routing: React Router or the routing solution supported by the generated project.
- Data: realistic sample data initially.
- Responsive support: desktop, tablet, and mobile.
- Browsers: current versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox, and Safari.

Lovable should preserve the existing project setup and use compatible dependencies rather than unnecessarily replacing the framework.

## 2.4 Design Constraints

- The application must maintain consistent navigation, typography, colors, spacing, and component styles.
- All important buttons must perform their intended actions.
- Forms must validate user input.
- Errors must be presented in clear and understandable language.
- Property information must be organized logically.
- Subscription prices and expiry conditions must be disclosed before confirmation.
- Simulated AI results must not be presented as genuine AI-generated results.
- Sample verification badges must not imply actual identity or property verification.
- All major workflows must remain usable on mobile devices.
- User data must not be exposed to unauthorized users in a production implementation.

## 2.5 Assumptions and Dependencies

- The initial version may use realistic demonstration listings.
- AI processing may be simulated until a real AI provider is integrated.
- Payments may be simulated for the prototype.
- Persistent accounts and messaging require a backend.
- Property authenticity and ownership require appropriate verification procedures.

