# 4. NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS

## 4.1 Usability

- NFR-USE-01: Navigation shall be understandable to first-time users.
- NFR-USE-02: Common tasks shall require as few unnecessary steps as practical.
- NFR-USE-03: Buttons shall use clear action-oriented labels.
- NFR-USE-04: Forms shall group related fields logically.
- NFR-USE-05: Users shall be able to recognize their current page or section.
- NFR-USE-06: The system shall use familiar interface patterns and consistent terminology.

## 4.2 Performance

- NFR-PERF-01: Local navigation and common interactions should respond promptly.
- NFR-PERF-02: Images shall be appropriately sized and optimized.
- NFR-PERF-03: Loading indicators shall appear during operations that take noticeable time.
- NFR-PERF-04: Large listing collections should use pagination or another suitable rendering strategy.

## 4.3 Security and Privacy

- NFR-SEC-01: Production authentication shall use a secure authentication provider or properly implemented server-side authentication.
- NFR-SEC-02: Passwords shall never be stored or transmitted as plain text in production.
- NFR-SEC-03: Production communication and sensitive information shall be transmitted over HTTPS.
- NFR-SEC-04: Protected actions shall be authorized on the server.
- NFR-SEC-05: Uploaded files shall be validated and safely handled.
- NFR-SEC-06: API secrets shall not be exposed in frontend code.
- NFR-SEC-07: Users shall only access data permitted by their roles.
- NFR-SEC-08: Payment credentials shall not be collected or stored by a simulated checkout interface.

## 4.4 Reliability

- NFR-REL-01: Common user actions shall have clear success or failure outcomes.
- NFR-REL-02: Invalid input shall not silently corrupt application state.
- NFR-REL-03: The interface shall handle missing data gracefully.
- NFR-REL-04: Repeated actions shall not create unintended duplicate records where persistence is implemented.

## 4.5 Accessibility

- NFR-ACC-01: Interface controls shall have accessible names.
- NFR-ACC-02: Forms shall have visible labels and understandable validation messages.
- NFR-ACC-03: Text and interactive controls shall maintain sufficient contrast.
- NFR-ACC-04: Important actions shall be operable using a keyboard.
- NFR-ACC-05: Focus indicators shall remain visible.
- NFR-ACC-06: Property photographs shall have meaningful alternative text.
- NFR-ACC-07: Information shall not be communicated through color alone.
- NFR-ACC-08: The interface should follow WCAG 2.2 Level AA guidelines where practical.

## 4.6 Compatibility

- NFR-COMP-01: The application shall support current major desktop and mobile browsers.
- NFR-COMP-02: Layouts shall adapt to different viewport sizes.
- NFR-COMP-03: Interactive elements shall remain usable on touchscreens.

## 4.7 Maintainability

- NFR-MAINT-01: Components shall be reusable where appropriate.
- NFR-MAINT-02: The codebase shall use a consistent naming convention.
- NFR-MAINT-03: Application routes and shared components shall be organized logically.
- NFR-MAINT-04: Mock data and service logic shall be separated from presentation components where practical.

