# 10. VALIDATION AND ERROR HANDLING

## 10.1 Form Validation

- Required fields shall not be submitted empty.
- Email fields shall validate email format.
- Password confirmation shall match the password entered.
- Maximum price shall not be less than minimum price.
- Price and area values shall not accept invalid negative values.
- Uploaded images shall comply with supported formats and file-size limits.
- Property forms shall require the essential listing information.
- Invalid fields shall display specific corrective messages.

## 10.2 Error States

The application shall provide understandable messages for:

- Invalid login details.
- Missing required fields.
- Failed image upload.
- No matching properties.
- Unavailable property records.
- Expired connections.
- Failed simulated transactions.
- Unauthorized access.
- Unexpected application errors.

Errors shall not expose stack traces, secrets, or internal implementation details to end users.

## 10.3 Confirmation States

The application shall provide confirmation after:

- Successful login or registration.
- Saving a favorite property.
- Saving or publishing a listing.
- Updating profile information.
- Completing a simulated subscription.
- Completing a supported design workflow.

Destructive actions shall display a confirmation dialog and provide a cancel option.

