# 11. PROTOTYPE IMPLEMENTATION REQUIREMENTS FOR LOVABLE

Lovable shall implement the requirements as a cohesive, interactive website rather than generating a collection of disconnected static screens.

## 11.1 Technology and Structure

- Use React and TypeScript with the project's existing compatible setup.
- Use Tailwind CSS and reusable components.
- Use a consistent icon library.
- Implement real client-side routing.
- Separate reusable UI components from page-specific logic.
- Maintain typed interfaces for properties, users, plans, and other data entities.
- Keep sample data separate from presentation components.
- Avoid unnecessary dependencies and duplicated code.

## 11.2 Prototype Functionality

The following interactions must work in the prototype:

- Navigation between all major screens.
- Property search and filtering using sample data.
- Property detail navigation.
- Saving and removing favorites.
- Property comparison.
- Matchmaker form validation and sample recommendations.
- Designer image upload and preview.
- Clearly labeled simulated design results when real AI is unavailable.
- Login and registration demonstration flows.
- Seller listing creation, editing, and deletion.
- Form validation and confirmation messages.
- Simulated subscription selection and expiry handling.
- Messaging demonstration and connection access restrictions.
- Responsive mobile navigation.

Use mock data and local state when appropriate. Browser storage may be used for non-sensitive demonstration persistence, but it must not be represented as secure authentication or production-grade storage.

## 11.3 AI Integration Rules

- Do not claim a real AI operation occurred when only mock results are displayed.
- Clearly label demonstration outputs.
- Keep API keys out of client-side code.
- If a genuine AI provider is integrated, use a secure backend or server-side function.
- Provide loading, success, and failure states for AI operations.

## 11.4 Payment Integration Rules

- The prototype shall simulate the plan-selection and confirmation workflow.
- No real payment shall be taken without explicit integration of a legitimate payment provider.
- Do not request actual card details in the simulated checkout.
- Display plan price, currency, duration, and expiry conditions before confirmation.

## 11.5 Responsive Design

- Desktop: use a structured multi-column layout where suitable.
- Tablet: reduce column counts while preserving readable content.
- Mobile: use single-column layouts for forms and property details where appropriate.
- Navigation shall adapt to small screens.
- Buttons and form controls shall be comfortable to operate by touch.
- Property images shall scale without distortion.
- Avoid horizontal overflow.

